esson 27: API Response Typing in TypeScript 🚀
Aaj hum seekhenge ki API se data aane par uska type kaise define karein aur data ko safely kaise handle karein.
1. API kya hoti hai?
Maan lo tumhari application server se user ki details mangti hai.
API response:
{
  "id": 1,
  "name": "Rahul",
  "email": "rahul@example.com"
}


TypeScript mein hum is data ka type define kar sakte hain.
type User = {
  id: number;
  name: string;
  email: string;
};


Ab TypeScript ko pata hai ki User object mein kaun-kaun si properties honi chahiye.
2. API se data fetch karna
type User = {
  id: number;
  name: string;
  email: string;
};

async function getUser(): Promise<User> {
  const response = await fetch(
    "https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users/1"
  );

  if (!response.ok) {
    throw new Error("API request failed");
  }

  const data: unknown = await response.json();

  if (
    typeof data === "object" &&
    data !== null &&
    "id" in data &&
    "name" in data &&
    "email" in data &&
    typeof data.id === "number" &&
    typeof data.name === "string" &&
    typeof data.email === "string"
  ) {
    return {
      id: data.id,
      name: data.name,
      email: data.email
    };
  }

  throw new Error("Invalid API response");
}

async function main(): Promise<void> {
  try {
    const user = await getUser();
    console.log(user.name);
    console.log(user.email);
  } catch (error: unknown) {
    if (error instanceof Error) {
      console.log(error.message);
    }
  }
}

main();


Is code mein kya ho raha hai?
- fetch() server se request karta hai.
- response.ok HTTP success status check karta hai.
- response.json() response body ko JavaScript value mein convert karta hai.
- unknown ke through data ko bina verify kiye trusted nahi maana.
- Type checks ke baad hi User object return kiya.
