3. Important difference: TypeScript type vs runtime validation
Ye code:
const user = await response.json() as User;


sirf TypeScript ko batata hai ki data User jaisa hai. Ye actual API response ko validate nahi karta.
Agar server galat data bheje, toh bhi assertion compile ho sakta hai. Isliye external data ko runtime par validate karna important hai.
